==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
All you need to do is send meatshields and semi-spammable attackers like [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]] and [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]] to defeat the enemy peons. However, the stage restrictions prevent most conventional meatshields, such as [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]], to be used, forcing the player to use more expensive tankers like [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] instead. When Spacefish Jones is isolated, just keep sending units who can resist a hit from it (e.g., [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]]) and you will be fine. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] will help you a lot here, due to his high damage and ability to stagger Spacefish Jones.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
The biggest challenge here is dealing with the Mistress Celeboodles and Scissoroos. Once you survive them all, you will be left alone with Spacefish Jones, which should be pretty easy to beat by itself. Make sure you bring something to deal with Kid Tappa's Barrier, such as a [[:Category:Barrier Breaker Cats|Barrier Breaker]] or a high-DPH unit, like Awakened Bahamut Cat.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
At the beginning of the level, use a fast unit to trigger the attack from the Axoloty. Once this is done, Axoloty becomes basically stationary, allowing you to focus on the Kid Tappa and the Scissoroos. Saving Awakened Bahamut to speed up the defeat of Axoloty will make this stage end quicker. Make sure you bring any unit with 15K DPH to deal with Kid Tappa's Barrier.

===='''Recommended Units'''====
*Island Cat: Due to the stage's restrictions, Island Cat is the best, most accessible option for a meatshield. With sufficient + levels (or a small Defense Up [[Cat Combo]]), Island Cat will be able to take a hit from Mistress Celeboodle before stunlocking it.
*[[Miter Saw Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Miter Saw Cat]]: Another option for a pseudo-meatshield, Miter Saw Cat is able to take on the Mistress Celeboodles with ease, and can also aid in taking down the Scissoroos.
*Awakened Bahamut: As a [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rusher]] with nuclear power attacks, Awakened Bahamut is an excellent and accessible option to rush down the Spacefish Jones/Axoloty.
*Ring Girl Cat/Pizza Cat: A tanky damage dealer that can take a hit from Mistress Celeboodle or Scissoroo before retaliating with solid damage of their own.
*Normal + Manic King Dragon Cat: Both are a good source of backline DPS against the Mistress Celeboodles/Scissoroos, helping to wear them down.
*[[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Major Leaguer Cat/Golfer Cat]]: One of the few non-Uber Barrier Breakers able to be used. With support from meatshields/tankers, he can potentially snipe the Spacefish Jones from afar.

